# SharedCLibrary's messages, in TAIRiX Bridge's own words.
NoMemory:The workspace is too small for the C library
UnknownChunk:The C library has no such chunk
StaticSize:A chunk's static data is not the size the C library's is
SwiRange:SWI value out of range for module %0
NotThirtyTwo:Application is not 32-bit compatible
NoApcsA:The C library no longer supports APCS-A
OutOfDate:The program needs a newer C library
UncaughtTrap:An uncaught trap, %0, at %1; its registers are at %2
DivideByZero:Divide by zero
StackOverflow:The stack could not be extended
NoMain:The program has no main program
Errno0:No error has been recorded
EDOM:EDOM - an argument outside the function's domain
ERANGE:ERANGE - a result outside the range its type holds
ESIGNUM:ESIGNUM - no such signal
EILSEQ:EILSEQ - not a valid multibyte character
EOVERFLOW:EOVERFLOW - a value too large for its type
EFBIG:EFBIG - the file would be too large
ErrnoUnknown:An error the C library does not know
FreeFailed:*** The run time system cannot carry on: free was given a block the heap does not hold
FreeOverwritten:*** The run time system cannot carry on: free was given a block whose header has been overwritten
HeapOverwritten:*** The run time system cannot carry on: the heap has been overwritten
Postmortem:Stack backtrace
BadAddress:(at address %0)
LibraryFrame:%0 in the shared C library
NamedFrame:%0 in function %1
UnnamedFrame:%0 in an unnamed function
Argument:  Argument %0: %1 %2
StackOverwritten:The stack has been overwritten
SignalAbort:The program has ended abnormally (abort() was called)
SignalIllegal:An illegal instruction (a call to something not a function, or overwritten code)
SignalAddress:An illegal address (perhaps far outside an array)
SignalInterrupt:The user interrupted the program, which has ended
SignalTerminate:The program was asked to end
SignalUnknown:Signal %0, which has no default action
AssertFailed:*** Assertion failed: %0, file %1, line %2
AssertFailedIn:*** Assertion failed: %0, function %1, file %2, line %3
ReadFail:A checked read outside the program's memory
WriteFail:A checked write outside the program's memory
MissingQuote:The command line has a double quote that is not closed
BadRedirection:The command line asks for an I/O redirection the C library cannot make
RedirectionFailed:%0 could not be opened for I/O redirection
NoArgumentsRoom:There is no room for the program's arguments
